{"page":1066,"blocks":[{"x":0.04849,"y":0.05257,"w":0.1403,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01535,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"AP-8 Appendices"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.09343,"w":0.04034,"h":0.01281,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"2. If"},{"x":0.5127,"y":0.11839,"w":0.21026,"h":0.0288,"fs":0.01279,"n":5,"k":0,"t":"1 21 + 1 22 + g + 1 2k = 1 - 1 2k,"},{"x":0.35277,"y":0.15995,"w":0.02817,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"then"},{"x":0.39192,"y":0.1759,"w":0.45175,"h":0.0378,"fs":0.01918,"n":12,"k":0,"t":"1 21 + 1 22 + g + 1 2k + 1 2k+1 = 1 - 1 2k + 1 2k+1 = 1 - 1 # 2 2k # 2 + 1 2k+1"},{"x":0.60636,"y":0.22454,"w":0.2215,"h":0.0288,"fs":0.01279,"n":7,"k":0,"t":"= 1 - 2 2k+1 + 1 2k+1 = 1 - 1 2k+1."},{"x":0.35277,"y":0.26542,"w":0.515,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Thus, the original formula holds for n = (k + 1) whenever it holds for n = k."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.28912,"w":0.59299,"h":0.02814,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"With these steps verified, the mathematical induction principle now guarantees the formula for every positive integer n."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.35654,"w":0.17484,"h":0.01375,"fs":0.01375,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"Other Starting Integers"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.38052,"w":0.59297,"h":0.02882,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Instead of starting at n = 1 some induction arguments start at another integer. The steps for such an argument are as follows."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.41889,"w":0.59305,"h":0.048,"fs":0.01279,"n":5,"k":1,"t":"1. Check that the formula holds for n = n1 (the first appropriate integer). 2. Prove that if the formula holds for any integer n = k Ú n1, then it also holds for n = (k + 1)."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.47712,"w":0.58893,"h":0.02966,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Once these steps are completed, the mathematical induction principle guarantees the for- mula for all n Ú n1."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.52913,"w":0.38006,"h":0.01449,"fs":0.01407,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"EXAMPLE 3 Show that n! 7 3n if n is large enough."},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.55683,"w":0.3777,"h":0.01365,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Solution How large is large enough? We experiment:"},{"x":0.41166,"y":0.5982,"w":0.41226,"h":0.05117,"fs":0.01279,"n":24,"k":0,"t":"n 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 n! 1 2 6 24 120 720 5040 3n 3 9 27 81 243 729 2187"},{"x":0.32331,"y":0.6758,"w":0.59308,"h":0.01422,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"It looks as if n! 7 3n for n Ú 7. To be sure, we apply mathematical induction. We take"},{"x":0.32414,"y":0.6919,"w":0.25038,"h":0.01535,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"n1 = 7 in Step 1 and complete Step 2."},{"x":0.35277,"y":0.7065,"w":0.26264,"h":0.01422,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"Suppose k! 7 3k for some k Ú 7. Then"},{"x":0.43799,"y":0.72195,"w":0.35961,"h":0.02238,"fs":0.01918,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"(k + 1)! = (k + 1)(k!) 7 (k + 1)3k 7 7 # 3k 7 3k+1."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.75329,"w":0.10998,"h":0.01347,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"Thus, for k Ú 7,"},{"x":0.49497,"y":0.7751,"w":0.24563,"h":0.01467,"fs":0.01279,"n":3,"k":0,"t":"k! 7 3k implies (k + 1)! 7 3k+1."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.79858,"w":0.50492,"h":0.01422,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"The mathematical induction principle now guarantees n! Ú 3n for all n Ú 7."},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.83674,"w":0.45954,"h":0.02909,"fs":0.01375,"n":2,"k":1,"t":"Proof of the Derivative Sum Rule for Sums of Finitely Many Functions"},{"x":0.32332,"y":0.87674,"w":0.15312,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"We prove the statement"},{"x":0.68197,"y":0.90542,"w":0.11587,"h":0.02975,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":0,"t":"dx + g + dun"},{"x":0.43775,"y":0.9055,"w":0.21663,"h":0.02968,"fs":0.01279,"n":2,"k":0,"t":"d dx (u1 + u2 + g + un) = du1"},{"x":0.6359,"y":0.9055,"w":0.06456,"h":0.02967,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx + du2"},{"x":0.7793,"y":0.92238,"w":0.01543,"h":0.01279,"fs":0.01279,"n":1,"k":1,"t":"dx"}]}